#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092019 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "3e096041-22f8-5b7e-88d7-eca10203a379" :question/math-academy-id "e-5470" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092020 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "e0f036c5-c27d-5a0e-aeb1-cb7c99b49691" :question/math-academy-id "e-5471" :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "53c7a748-dadb-516e-879b-92cd0c986041" :question/math-academy-id "e-7454" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c96d7f2-1ee7-5791-9ae5-bdbe9213f7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c96d7f2-1ee7-5791-9ae5-bdbe9213f7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283988} :answer-field/id #uuid "143db726-05fb-5d0a-a155-0badb129e056" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b294812-bbb1-576e-90e7-b71f935c112b" :question/math-academy-id "q-275796" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =|5-8| \\\\  & =|-3| \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eae7a4c-f31a-5607-8fbd-a4bec1063d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283998} {:answer/id #uuid "fad23fc3-448c-5f26-9534-b12393665062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fad23fc3-448c-5f26-9534-b12393665062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283999} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ceac146-cb19-5420-beed-d1da2ba376d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "195a297e-9cc0-5f3c-a791-702692fd25d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-316578" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|8\\cdot 2-7\\cdot (-3)| \\\\  & =|16-(-21)| \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c466f5-12a2-5326-8360-dbac1c75312e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c466f5-12a2-5326-8360-dbac1c75312e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284006} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2dd50da-f51e-570d-a033-74dc33383755" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bca98248-d03b-5f6b-b96d-7295f22821a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316591" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/455e0a08e2a0929a60d7fa1b76973e1b7a460efe8cc1cf01719ce211feacd8c0.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e7464d-7629-5806-aa07-04e5640e39cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284009} {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c99caa6-f201-5a73-979b-5074f5344bf3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d412caa5-3690-592c-8eec-aa466eedc1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316606" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1),(5,1),(3,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/3e2c56766f201095bee0eea101b877e30910c676c998f37d261fd7cf7aabb837.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758a80e2-fef0-5d0c-9131-acf560683f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "758a80e2-fef0-5d0c-9131-acf560683f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284013} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a06e39e-da10-5b2b-801f-8c68b17f7337" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "423d63ac-43bc-545e-9007-0b2aae970538" :question/math-academy-id "q-316607" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(0,0),(6,0),(2,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/059560835586e9c149cdb5dabcddc80610a58bfa0c30cb5f685b8bb6bdca3e90.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5=15.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "706f557a-719f-52f6-9e63-2d3f4b2d9d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284033} {:answer/id #uuid "5b50e6e2-80aa-5a06-9b77-0391e59a6f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284034} {:answer/id #uuid "55e29dc6-9969-527f-814b-5543bd045230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284035} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef67f89-9929-56ca-b481-9b7c306ac8c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284036} {:answer/id #uuid "71726a20-fe1d-5adc-bdeb-0b79ddcd9258" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/re